# Geared Motor Selection

## 1. Drive Requirements

Based on the previous drive calculation, the preliminary requirements
for the conveyor drive are:

- Belt speed: 0.3 m/s
- Drive pulley diameter: 80 mm
- Required output speed: about 72 rpm
- Theoretical torque: 2.11 Nm
- Preliminary design torque: 3.72 Nm
- Theoretical power: 15.8 W
- Preliminary design power: 27.9 W

The conveyor operates horizontally and transports a maximum load of 20 kg.
## 2. Motor Selection Criteria

The geared motor should meet the following criteria:

- Motor power higher than the calculated design power
- Output speed close to 72 rpm
- Output torque higher than 3.72 Nm
- Suitable gear ratio
- Suitable mounting configuration for the conveyor
- Sufficient service factor

## 3. Candidate 1 - SEW-EURODRIVE R Series
One suitable configuration found in the SEW DriveConfigurator was:

- Type: R07DRN63MS4
- Rated motor power: 0.12 kW
- Output speed: 75 rpm
- Output torque: 15 Nm
- Gear ratio: 18.31
- Motor speed: 1380 rpm
- Service factor fB: 3.3

The output speed of 75 rpm is close to the calculated target
speed of approximately 72 rpm.

The output torque of 15 Nm is also higher than the preliminary
required design torque of 3.72 Nm.
